  "body": "Independently classify all 720 paired source/target relabelings of each of the eight mutable-leaver cells in the selected PR1042 scalar word. Every cell has 36 dirt-preserving labelings and 48 exact fixed-label-span-boundary labelings, but only 6 satisfy both. All 5,760 retain the clean transfer. Explicit witnesses show why either filter alone is insufficient.\n\nThe source is the selected replay archive's R480 seven-slot word, not its inherited R492 evidence. A separate column-transport and explicit binary-span implementation reconstructs entry states and verifies the complete census. The fixed actual entry/exit label-span model includes closing rank increments; this is a local label-span boundary atlas, not a replacement supplier or new kappa.\n\nCredit: LeaverSAT/LeaverSAT2, icekylinx and the PR1004/1005/1018 lineage; thakrarsagar's PR1049 already covers the selected cells' endpoint audit. Contributor @woklerx with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. Apache-2.0.\n\nReproduce:\n\n```\npython -I -O -B research/leaver-relabel-atlas-seed81/verify.py\npython -I -O -B research/leaver-relabel-atlas-seed81/test_package.py\n```\n\nNo native, phase, provider, precision or outer-invoice replay. No circuit optimum, profile saving, composed relabelings or independent human review claimed.\n\nThe label-span test does not check Gram-form or residual legality. Six labelings pass both tested filters; this is not sufficient evidence of native frame admission.\n",
